  "description": "RUGSUH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H130 O38 P2 Pr8. From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 7 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr4 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr3B (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr1B (Pr) has 7 O neighbors; Pr2B (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr4B (Pr) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.603-5.183 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.16-161.73°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Pr4(μ4-O)2(μ3,η2-OR)2(μ,η2-OR)4(μ,η1-OR)(OR)(OPMe3)]2 (R = C2H4OMe); C54H130O38P2Pr8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
